msgid "Add a computer"
msgstr "Añadir un ordenador"

#: __app.rb:1584
msgid "Add a new computer in this place"
msgstr ""

#: games/krowa_support/presentation.rb:58
msgid "Add noun to dictionary and check"
msgstr "Añadir el sustantivo al diccionario y comprobar"

#: lib/table_activity_repository.rb:182
msgid "Added %{bot} at %{owner}'s table for %{game}."
msgstr "Se ha añadido a %{bot} a la mesa de %{owner} (%{game})."

#: lib/table_activity_repository.rb:197
msgid "Added %{bot}."
msgstr "Se ha añadido a %{bot}."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:275
msgid "Added 3-5-8 by Guliwer777: a card game for three players, with trick-taking, contract selection and card exchanges between deals. You can also play against bots."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:239
msgid "Added Audio Ball by budyn1211, known on ELTEN as balteam: an audio game for two players, against another person or a bot. Recognize three shot sounds, choose the matching defence and prepare your return. Sets are played to seven points with a two-point lead; choose one, two or three sets to win."
msgstr "Se ha añadido Audio Ball, de budyn1211, conocido en ELTEN como balteam: un juego de audio para dos jugadores, contra otra persona o un bot. Reconoce tres sonidos de golpe, elige la defensa correspondiente y prepara la devolución. Los sets se juegan a siete puntos, con dos de ventaja; elige si hay que ganar uno, dos o tres sets."

msgid "Added Audio Ball by budyn1211: an audio game for two players, against another person or a bot. Recognize three shot sounds, choose the matching defence and prepare your return. Sets are played to seven points with a two-point lead; choose one, two or three sets to win."
msgstr "Se ha añadido Audio Ball, de budyn1211: un juego de audio para dos jugadores, contra otra persona o un bot. Reconoce tres sonidos de golpe, elige la defensa correspondiente y prepara la devolución. Los sets se juegan a siete puntos, con dos de ventaja; elige si hay que ganar uno, dos o tres sets."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:185
msgid "Added Axel Pong Doubles by budyn1211: two teams of two players, with alternating returns and shared scores. Spectators can use 1–4 to choose a player's perspective. Partners have distinguishable step and return sounds."
msgstr "Se ha añadido el modo Dobles de Axel Pong, de budyn1211: dos equipos de dos jugadores, con devoluciones alternas y puntuaciones compartidas. Los espectadores pueden usar 1–4 para elegir la perspectiva de un jugador. Los pasos y las devoluciones de los compañeros de equipo tienen sonidos que permiten distinguirlos."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:170
msgid "Added Axel Pong, an audio ping-pong game for two people or a player and a bot, with Classic and Arcade Classic modes and six difficulty levels. Play with the keyboard or mouse. Ctrl+P at the table opens personal settings for automatic return and sound volumes, also available in Settings > Axel Pong."
msgstr "Se ha añadido Axel Pong, un juego de ping-pong sonoro para dos personas o una persona y un bot, con los modos Clásico y Arcade Clásico y seis niveles de dificultad. Juega con el teclado o el ratón. Ctrl+P en la mesa abre los ajustes personales de devolución automática y de volumen de los sonidos, también disponibles en Ajustes > Axel Pong."

msgid "Added Axel Pong: follow the ball by sound, move your paddle and return it to your opponent. Play against another person or a bot, with six difficulty levels and a target of 7, 11 or 21 points, won by a two-point lead. Choose Classic or Arcade Classic, which adds temporary shields and an invisible ball."
msgstr "Se ha añadido Axel Pong: sigue la pelota por el sonido, mueve tu pala y devuélvela al oponente. Juega contra otra persona o un bot, con seis niveles de dificultad y un objetivo de 7, 11 o 21 puntos, con dos puntos de ventaja para ganar. Elige Clásico o Arcade Clásico, que añade escudos temporales y una pelota invisible."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:141
msgid "Added Battleship by Dawid Pieper: two fleets, manual placement, a computer opponent, spectator boards and a final fleet check. Saving this game for later is not yet available."
msgstr "Se ha añadido Hundir la flota, de Dawid Pieper: dos flotas, colocación manual, un oponente controlado por el ordenador, tableros para espectadores y una comprobación final de las flotas. Todavía no se puede guardar esta partida para continuarla más tarde."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:202
msgid "Added Cat, head, tail by TD Programs: a dice game for 2–8 players. Roll an eight-sided die and decide when to bank your points. Includes bots and Polish and English rules."
msgstr "Se ha añadido Gato, cabeza, cola, de TD Programs: un juego de dados para 2–8 jugadores. Lanza un dado de ocho caras y decide cuándo guardar tus puntos. Incluye bots y reglas en polaco e inglés."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:276
msgid "Added Czech and Spanish interface translations by balteam. Choose the language in Settings > General. These translations do not include game rules. Tysiac is now called 1000 card game in English."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:147
msgid "Added Krowa by paulinux: guess Polish words in the daily puzzle, solo play, Race or cooperative Word Tower, with a personal gallery and optional leaderboards."
msgstr "Se ha añadido Krowa, de paulinux: adivina palabras en polaco en el desafío diario, en solitario, en Carrera o en el modo cooperativo Torre de palabras, con una galería personal y clasificaciones opcionales."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:142
msgid "Added Mancala by Dawid Pieper, with Oware, Ayoayo and Kalah variants and three computer strengths. Both new games include clear Polish and English rules, keyboard help and move sounds."
msgstr "Se ha añadido Mancala, de Dawid Pieper, con las variantes Oware, Ayoayo y Kalah y tres niveles de dificultad del ordenador. Ambos juegos nuevos incluyen reglas claras en polaco e inglés, ayuda sobre los atajos de teclado y sonidos de los movimientos."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:274
msgid "Added War and Scientific War by balteam, for two to eight players, with bots. War compares cards from a face-down deck; Scientific War lets you choose your cards and use their special powers."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:177
msgid "Added a Draw another word button to Krowa's Random word variant. It reveals the previous word and resets attempts without recording a win."
msgstr "Se ha añadido el botón Elegir otra palabra al azar a la variante Palabra aleatoria de Krowa. Revela la palabra anterior y reinicia los intentos sin registrar una victoria."

msgid "Added a test adaptation of Axel Pong: follow the ball by sound, move your paddle and return it to your opponent. Play against another person or a bot, with six difficulty levels and a target of 7, 11 or 21 points, won by a two-point lead."
msgstr "Se ha añadido una adaptación de prueba de Axel Pong: sigue la pelota por el sonido, mueve tu pala y devuélvela al oponente. Juega contra otra persona o un bot, con seis niveles de dificultad y un objetivo de 7, 11 o 21 puntos, con dos puntos de ventaja para ganar."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:265
msgid "Added missing Polish messages, including the notice that Daily Krowa requires a private table."
msgstr "Se han añadido mensajes que faltaban en polaco, incluido el aviso de que Krowa diaria requiere una mesa privada."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:128
msgid "Added sounds for banking points in Farkle, reaching exactly 33 or 66 in 99, and declaring a marriage in Tysiac."
msgstr "Se han añadido sonidos al guardar puntos en Farkle, alcanzar exactamente 33 o 66 en 99 y realizar un anuncio en Mil."

#: __app.rb:1486
msgid "Adding computer"
msgstr "Añadiendo un ordenador"

#: games/yahtzee.rb:289
msgid "Additional Yahtzee bonuses: %{points}."
msgstr "Bonificaciones por Yahtzees adicionales: %{points}."

msgid "Adnan Menderes Hava alani"
msgstr "Adnan Menderes Hava alani"

msgid "Advance to Start and collect %{amount}."
msgstr "Avanza hasta la Salida y cobra %{amount}."

#: games/uno.rb:147
msgid "Advanced responses"
msgstr "Respuestas avanzadas"

#: games/uno.rb:107
msgid "Advanced responses requires ordinary responses and is off by default. Skip or Wild passes the debt onwards; Reverse sends it in the other direction. In No Mercy, Discard All and Skip Everyone instead cancel a pending numerical drawing penalty."
msgstr ""

msgid "Aerodrom Car Konstantin - Niš"
msgstr "Aerodrom Car Konstantin - Niš"

msgid "Aerodrom Nikola Tesla - Beograd"
msgstr "Aerodrom Nikola Tesla - Beograd"

msgid "Aeroportul Internaţional Henri Coandă"
msgstr "Aeroportul Internaţional Henri Coandă"

msgid "After a Pong point, key presses from the break no longer serve the next ball by themselves. Fixed an error when a new rally had not arrived yet, and clarified the first-serve announcements. Two human players wait until both sides are ready; a bot match does not use that initial countdown."
msgstr "Tras un punto en Pong, las pulsaciones realizadas durante la pausa ya no provocan por sí solas el saque de la siguiente pelota. Se ha corregido un error que se producía cuando aún no había llegado el nuevo intercambio y se han aclarado los avisos del primer saque. Cuando juegan dos personas, se espera hasta que ambas estén listas; las partidas contra un bot no utilizan esa cuenta atrás inicial."

#: games/poker.rb:23
msgid "After a number of hands"
msgstr "Tras un número de repartos"

#: games/poker.rb:24
msgid "After a number of minutes"
msgstr "Tras un número de minutos"

#: games/audio_ball.rb:211
msgid "After a point, the game plays an announcement and reads the score: yours first, then your opponent's. When needed, speech synthesis replaces the recorded score announcement. Observers hear the scores in the order of players at the table."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:22
msgid "After a second review, 284 well-supported Quiz Party questions were restored without bringing back ambiguous questions."
msgstr "Tras una segunda revisión, se han recuperado 284 preguntas de Quiz Party bien documentadas, sin volver a incluir preguntas ambiguas."

#: games/krowa_support/presentation.rb:26
msgid "After a word ends, the solution is revealed. The Word definition button opens its SJP description; a missing description also remains readable."
msgstr ""

#: games/three_five_eight.rb:82
msgid "After any exchanges, the chooser reveals the four-card kitty, adds it to their hand and discards four cards face down. The chooser leads the first trick. The winner of every trick leads the next one."
msgstr ""

msgid "After completing the shared track, each player enters a private six-field home lane. Reaching its end places the pawn at the finish, where it no longer moves."
msgstr ""

msgid "After defending, you hold the ball. Press Right arrow or A to prepare, then press one of the three shot keys to hit. The server must also prepare before serving. A defence only catches the ball: it does not automatically send it back. An attack does not select the lane for a later incoming ball. Keep focus on the Audio Ball playfield when using these controls. Each new attack needs a fresh press; a selected defensive lane or a key still held after preparation does not hit automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "After defending, you hold the ball. Press Right arrow or A to prepare, then press one of the three shot keys to hit. The server must also prepare before serving. A defence only catches the ball: it does not automatically send it back. Keep focus on the Audio Ball playfield when using these controls."
msgstr ""

msgid "After defending, you hold the ball. Press Right arrow or A to prepare, then press one of the three shot keys to hit. The server must also prepare before serving. A defence only catches the ball: it does not automatically send it back. Keep focus on the Audio Ball playfield when using these controls. Each new attack needs a fresh press; keeping the defense key held after preparation does not hit automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "After defending, you hold the ball. Press Right arrow or A to prepare, then press one of the three shot keys to hit. The server must also prepare before serving. A defence only catches the ball: it does not automatically send it back. The shot key also selects your lane for the next defence. Keep focus on the Audio Ball playfield when using these controls. Each new attack needs a fresh press; a selected lane or a key still held after preparation does not hit automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "After drawing a penalty, your turn also ends if you have no playable card. If skipping after a penalty is enabled, the turn always ends."
msgstr ""

msgid "After each turn, everyone may inspect the used cards. The table master can change a card to guessed, skipped, violation or no points, after discussing disputes. Corrections remain in the history. The master must approve the review before the next turn. Approved scores cannot be edited. A technical restart cancels the whole turn's points and repeats the same describing player with new cards; previously revealed cards stay used."
msgstr ""

msgid "After every round the scores are updated and another deal begins automatically while no unique leader has reached the selected limit. Once there is such a leader, that player or team wins the game."
msgstr ""

msgid "After every selected match is complete, the player with the highest combined score wins."
msgstr ""

#: games/quiz_party.rb:85
msgid "After everyone answers or time expires, the game reveals the answers and awards points, then prepares the next question. Preparing a question is not another answer choice: wait for the new question to appear. Once all three have been settled, the round summary is available and the next category selection begins unless the match has ended."
msgstr ""

#: games/mancala.rb:68
msgid "After gathering the remaining seeds, compare the stores. More seeds wins and equal stores mean a draw. Unlike Oware, Ayoayo does not stop merely because someone has passed half of the total."
msgstr ""

msgid "After giving the cards, the taker may raise the contract within the legal limit based on the marriages still in hand. Playing the first card accepts the current contract without another mandatory bidding step."
msgstr ""

msgid "After keeping a combination, choose either Roll N dice or, once the required minimum has been reached, Bank X points. Rolling continues the same turn with the remaining dice; banking makes the turn points permanent and passes play to the next player."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:25
msgid "After playing Wild or Wild Draw Four in UNO, colours are offered in the order yellow, red, blue, green."
msgstr "Tras jugar un comodín o un comodín roba cuatro en UNO, los colores se ofrecen en este orden: amarillo, rojo, azul, verde."

msgid "After seeing the talon and before giving away a card, the bidder may surrender unless already on the barrel. The bidder receives zero and each defender receives at least 60 points, or half the contract when that is higher, rounded upward to a multiple of 5. The first 2 surrenders are free; every third surrender costs the bidder 120 points."
msgstr ""

#: games/tysiac.rb:100
msgid "After seeing the talon but before giving away or setting aside the first card, the bidder may surrender, unless on the barrel. Each defender receives at least 60, or half the contract if that is higher, rounded upwards to five. With two players there is only one defender, receiving the same award. No last-trick award applies to a surrendered deal. The bidder normally receives zero. Every third surrender additionally costs the bidder 120 points."
msgstr ""

msgid "After seeing the talon but before giving away the first card, the bidder may surrender, unless on the barrel. Each defender receives at least 60, or half the contract if that is higher, rounded upwards to five. The bidder normally receives zero. Every third surrender additionally costs the bidder 120 points."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:145
msgid "After selecting a game to create a table, focus starts on the opening instructions again. Tab then moves to Private table and the game settings."
msgstr "Tras seleccionar un juego para crear una mesa, el foco vuelve a situarse en las instrucciones iniciales. A continuación, Tab lleva a Mesa privada y a los ajustes del juego."

#: games/three_five_eight.rb:93
msgid "After the eighteenth deal, the player with the highest total score wins. Equal highest totals produce a shared draw."
msgstr ""

#: games/tysiac.rb:90
msgid "After the first trick, a player leading a trick may declare a marriage by playing its king or queen while still holding the matching partner. The declared suit becomes trump immediately. Hearts add 100 points, diamonds 80, clubs 60 and spades 40. A later marriage changes trump again. Simply owning the pair, or playing it without the declaration, does not award that bonus."
msgstr ""

#: games/biblios.rb:71
msgid "After the last auction is settled, total each player's cards in every category. The highest total wins that category's die. A tied total is decided by the card letter closest to A in that category. A category nobody holds awards nothing. Add the faces of the dice you won to obtain your victory points; card values themselves are not added again."
msgstr ""

#: games/audio_ball.rb:193
msgid "After the opponent hits, listen to the ball and press the matching defence key once. You may press it as soon as you recognise the sound, then release it. That choice remains active for this incoming ball, and you catch it automatically within the final two steps of the court. You do not need to time another press at contact. If you choose the wrong direction, you can correct it before the ball passes you; the last direction you choose is the one that counts."
msgstr ""

msgid "After the shared track a pawn enters its own six-field home lane; opponents cannot enter that lane. The last field is the finish. A pawn at the finish no longer moves and is not offered as a playable pawn."
msgstr ""

msgid "After the turn ends, other players must cover the most recently left unfinished double first, even on a normally closed train. They cannot play elsewhere until it is covered. Uncovered older doubles then remain for the following players, in reverse order. Failure to answer requires one draw, then opening your own train and passing if no answer exists. The obligation stays on the table."
msgstr ""

#: games/taboo_ui.rb:88
msgid "After time expires, everyone may inspect the cards used in that turn. Discuss disputed decisions, then the table master can change a result to guessed, skipped, violation or no points. Changes appear in the history. The master must approve the review before play continues; approved turns cannot be edited later."
msgstr ""

#: games/biblios.rb:59
msgid "After you finish distributing, the other players each choose one public card, starting with the next seat. In a four-player game, you therefore keep one, reserve one for auction and let the other three players choose from the three public cards. Then the next player distributes gifts. Continue until the gift deck is exhausted."
msgstr ""

msgid "After your first meld you can replace a table joker with its actual natural card from your hand. No separate Recover joker menu item is needed. In a three-card set with a joker and two suits, first add a third natural suit; only the fourth missing suit then recovers the joker. A bare joker cannot be appended to an existing meld."
msgstr ""

#: games/rummy_ui.rb:127
msgid "After your first meld, you can recover a table joker by playing the natural card needed in its place. This is a use of the replacement card, not a separate command on the joker. In a three-card set with two natural suits and a joker, first add a third natural suit; the remaining fourth suit can then replace the joker. You cannot simply pull out a joker and leave an invalid combination behind."
msgstr ""

msgid "Agra Station"
msgstr "Estación de Agra"

#: lib/game_history_navigation.rb:129
msgid "All"
msgstr "Todo"

#: lib/game_room_ui.rb:24
msgid "All Game Room sounds"
msgstr "Todos los sonidos de Game Room"

#: games/uno.rb:798
msgid "All active players pass their hands to the next player in seating order."
msgstr "Todos los jugadores activos pasan sus manos al siguiente jugador según el orden de los asientos."

#: games/uno.rb:798
msgid "All active players pass their hands to the previous player in seating order."
msgstr "Todos los jugadores activos pasan sus manos al jugador anterior según el orden de los asientos."

msgid "All active players passed their hands on."
msgstr "Todos los jugadores activos han pasado sus manos al siguiente jugador."

#: games/makao.rb:479
msgid "All cards in a packet must have the same value."
msgstr "Todas las cartas de un grupo deben tener el mismo valor."

msgid "All history"
msgstr "Todo el historial"

#: games/poker.rb:1203
msgid "All in; %{amount}"
msgstr "Todo apostado; %{amount}"

msgid "All options appear in one table form. Length applies to Random word and Race, while scoring applies only to Race. Daily Krowa and Word Tower ignore those fields."
msgstr ""

#: games/ludo.rb:266
msgid "All pawns"
msgstr "Todas las fichas"

#: games/farkle.rb:536
msgid "All six dice scored; hot dice."
msgstr "Los seis dados han puntuado; dados calientes."

msgid "All-in commits your remaining chips if the betting structure permits it. It does not itself end the game or automatically win the hand. Players with chips still respond. A short all-in below a full raise does not reopen raising for players who already acted, unless cumulative increases reach the required amount. If further betting is impossible, remaining community cards are dealt and the hand is settled."
msgstr ""

#: games/poker.rb:91
msgid "All-in puts in your remaining chips, subject to the betting limits. Other players still have to respond. If you cannot afford a full call, you may call with everything you have. An all-in smaller than a full raise does not normally let players who already acted raise again; several small increases must add up to a full raise before that right returns. If nobody can continue betting, the game completes the board where needed and compares the hands."
msgstr ""

#: games/categories.rb:187
msgid "Allow a shared victory"
msgstr "Permitir una victoria compartida"

#: games/uno.rb:149
msgid "Allow challenging Wild Draw Four"
msgstr "Permitir desafiar el comodín roba cuatro"

#: games/mexican_train.rb:114
msgid "Allow drawing even when having a playable piece is off by default. Enabling it lets you draw voluntarily before playing. You still get only one draw for the current decision, not repeated draws by pressing Space. After playing a double and gaining another decision, you may draw once again if needed. Drawing does not let you ignore an unfinished double."
msgstr ""

#: games/domino.rb:150
msgid "Allow drawing even when having a playable piece is on by default. Turn it off to require playing a tile you already hold whenever possible. Draw until finding a playable piece is separately off: when enabled, one Space draws a batch ending at the first newly drawn playable tile or an empty boneyard. It is still one drawing action, not many separate turns."
msgstr ""

#: games/makao.rb:137 games/uno.rb:152
msgid "Allow drawing with a playable card"
msgstr "Permitir robar aunque tengas una carta que puedas jugar"

#: games/uno.rb:100
msgid "Allow drawing with a playable card is on by default. Its separate limit is normally three voluntary cards per turn, from one to twenty. At the limit, another press only reports that you cannot draw; it does not secretly end the turn. If optional drawing is off, having a legal card prevents an ordinary draw."
msgstr ""

#: games/domino.rb:32 games/mexican_train.rb:14
msgid "Allow drawing with a playable tile"
msgstr "Permitir robar aunque se tenga una ficha que se pueda jugar"

msgid "Allow drawing with a playable tile defaults to off. When enabled, one voluntary draw is permitted in the current decision; existing legal tiles remain playable even if the new one does not fit. It does not permit ignoring a required double. After playing a double you receive a new decision, with at most one new draw. Repeated Space without playing cannot draw repeatedly. There is no thinking-time setting or team mode."
msgstr ""

msgid "Allow drawing with a playable tile is on by default. Drawing never removes the right to play a legal tile already held. Without a legal move after drawing the turn ends. Forbid drawing disables both drawing options; an empty or forbidden boneyard and no legal tile cause an automatic pass."
msgstr ""

#: games/poker.rb:158
msgid "Allow exchanging all five cards"
msgstr "Permitir cambiar las cinco cartas"

#: games/reversi.rb:30
msgid "Allow passing even when a move exists"
msgstr "Permitir pasar aunque haya un movimiento posible"

#: games/reversi.rb:54
msgid "Allow passing is also enabled by default. It lets you give the turn to your opponent even when you have a legal move. You may do this repeatedly; voluntary passes alone do not produce a draw. Switch the option off if you want players to pass only when they cannot place a disc."
msgstr ""

msgid "Allow passing is on by default. P gives your turn to the opponent even if you can place a disc. There is no limit on voluntary passes and repeated passes do not end the game. When passing is disabled, a turn is skipped only if no placement is possible. A full board or no possible placement for either player ends the game: more discs wins, equal numbers draw. Old saved games retain their original rules."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_surfaces/word_board.rb:72
msgid "Alphabetical rack order."
msgstr "Atril en orden alfabético."

#: games/scientific_war.rb:816
msgid "Already chosen: %{players}."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:75 lib/game_room_changelog.rb:97
msgid "Also added Biblios by dawidpieper (Pajper): a card game of building a library and bidding at auctions, for two to four players, with bots and Polish translation."
msgstr "También se ha añadido Biblios, de dawidpieper (Pajper): un juego de cartas en el que construyes una biblioteca y pujas en subastas, para entre dos y cuatro jugadores, con bots y traducción al polaco."

#: __app.rb:681 lib/game_shortcut_bindings.rb:60
msgid "Alt"
msgstr "Alt"

msgid "American / Atlantic City is the default. Each board changes field names and can change the layout, currency, starting capital, salary, building prices and bank supply. Larger boards have additional colour groups, up to six stations and four utilities. The details below describe the data actually used by this program, not a promise of identical economics in every published Monopoly edition."
msgstr ""

#: content/monopoly_boards.rb:10
msgid "American board / Atlantic City"
msgstr "Tablero estadounidense / Atlantic City"

#: games/ninety_nine.rb:83
msgid "An ace gives you a choice of adding 1 or 11. A ten lets you add or subtract 10, but you cannot go below zero. The game asks for that choice before playing the card."
msgstr ""

#: games/tysiac.rb:92
msgid "An ace is worth 11, a ten 10, a king four, a queen three, a jack two and a nine zero. The cards total 120 points. Add any declared marriages before checking the bidder's contract."
msgstr ""

msgid "An empty hand wins the round for zero points. Other players add their remaining pips; double blank is always ten, even alongside other tiles. With an empty boneyard, a complete circuit without a legal play blocks the round and everyone scores their hand. Opening a train may create a move for an earlier player, so a pass counter alone does not end the round."
msgstr ""

#: games/ludo.rb:55
msgid "An exact roll is required to reach the finish"
msgstr "Se necesita una tirada exacta para llegar a la meta"

#: games/ludo.rb:77
msgid "An exact roll is required to reach the finish is on by default. A pawn two squares from the finish needs a two: a larger result cannot move it. With this option off, an overshooting roll also takes the pawn to the finish."
msgstr ""

msgid "An exact roll is required to reach the finish: on by default. A roll going past the finish cannot move that pawn. When disabled, an excessive roll also brings it to the finish. Three consecutive sixes lose the turn: on by default; the third six ends the turn without moving a pawn for that roll, but does not undo previous moves."
msgstr ""

#: __app.rb:1660
msgid "An invitation to this table is already pending for this user."
msgstr "Este usuario ya tiene una invitación pendiente para esta mesa."

#: games/krowa.rb:282
msgid "An observer does not take part in the game."
msgstr "Un espectador no participa en la partida."

#: games/axel_pong.rb:277
msgid "An opponent who does not serve"
msgstr ""

#: games/uno.rb:99
msgid "An ordinary draw takes one card. If you still have no legal card afterwards, your turn ends automatically. Otherwise you may play. When the pile runs out, discards except the top card are shuffled back for drawing; nobody loses their hand."
msgstr ""

msgid "An uninterrupted line of at least four of your pieces horizontally, vertically or diagonally wins immediately. Filling all 42 fields without a winning line is a draw. This game has no configurable rule variants or board sizes. Both people and computers can play."
msgstr ""

#: games/monopoly.rb:62
msgid "An unowned street, station or utility may be bought when you land on it. The game gives its name, colour or type, and price. If you have enough cash, choose whether to buy. If you cannot afford it, the purchase is declined automatically. A property you do not buy remains available, unless the auction option sends it to auction."
msgstr ""

#: games/categories.rb:1329
msgid "Animal"
msgstr "Animal"

msgid "Announce lobby changes"
msgstr "Anunciar los cambios en la sala de espera"

#: lib/game_room_screens.rb:192
msgid "Announce when a computer is added or removed"
msgstr "Anunciar cuando se añada o se elimine un ordenador"

#: lib/game_room_screens.rb:184
msgid "Announce when a player joins a table"
msgstr "Anunciar cuando un jugador se una a una mesa"

#: lib/game_room_screens.rb:188
msgid "Announce when a player leaves a table"
msgstr "Anunciar cuando un jugador salga de una mesa"

#: lib/game_room_screens.rb:180
msgid "Announce when a table is created"
msgstr "Anunciar cuando se cree una mesa"

#: lib/axel_pong/settings.rb:17
msgid "Announcer volume"
msgstr "Volumen del locutor"

#: games/krowa.rb:281
msgid "Another person is playing now."
msgstr "Ahora está jugando otra persona."

#: games/krowa.rb:285
msgid "Another word has already started."
msgstr "Ya se ha empezado otra palabra."

#: games/categories.rb:129
msgid "Answer language"
msgstr "Idioma de las respuestas"

msgid "Answer language is Polish by default, with English also available. It chooses the alphabet used for drawing letters, not each player's interface language. Used letters are avoided until the selected alphabet has been exhausted. Category names are displayed in the player's interface language."
msgstr ""

#: games/categories.rb:94
msgid "Answer language is Polish by default; English is also available. It chooses the alphabet for letter draws and the language you agree to answer in, not the interface language. Category labels follow your interface. Letters do not repeat until the selected alphabet has been used up."
msgstr ""

msgid "Answer questions correctly to earn points. Speed does not affect the score, provided you answer before the time expires."
msgstr ""

#: games/quiz_party.rb:89
msgid "Answer time and the finishing line"
msgstr ""

msgid "Answer time and the judge"
msgstr ""

#: games/categories.rb:99
msgid "Answer time defaults to 90 seconds. Set zero for unlimited time, or 10–3600 seconds. Only writing is timed, not judging. Near the deadline the game warns you; at the deadline it submits the text still in your fields rather than clearing it first. A participant whose answers do not arrive during closing is treated as having empty entries. Without a time limit, all answering players must submit to move on."
msgstr ""

msgid "Answer time defaults to 90 seconds. Use 0 for no limit, or 10 to 3600 seconds. The countdown applies to writing, not to judging; without a limit everyone must submit. Local announcements warn near the end and announce expiry."
msgstr ""

#: games/krowa_support/presentation.rb:63
msgid "Answer: %{length} letters"
msgstr "Respuesta: %{length} letras"

msgid "Answering"
msgstr "Respondiendo"

msgid "Answering and judging keys"
msgstr "Teclas para responder y evaluar"

#: games/categories.rb:312
msgid "Answering has closed."
msgstr "Se ha cerrado el plazo para responder."

msgid "Answers are hidden while anyone is still writing. When everyone submits, or time expires, writing closes and submitted answers become available for judging. At the deadline the program submits the text still in your fields; it does not first clear it. A participant who has not supplied answers within closing is treated as having empty answers."
msgstr ""

msgid "Answers remain hidden until writing has closed. If a time limit is enabled, missing answers become blank when the time expires. The table master can also close answering manually."
msgstr ""

msgid "Answers remain hidden until writing has closed. Writing closes after every player submits or, when a time limit is enabled, when that time expires; missing answers then become blank."
msgstr ""

#: games/poker.rb:144
msgid "Ante in five-card draw"
msgstr "Ante en el póquer con descarte de cinco cartas"

#: games/uno.rb:1526
msgid "Any colour may be played."
msgstr "Se puede jugar cualquier color."

msgid "Apeadero Paseo de Gracia"
msgstr "Apeadero Paseo de Gracia"

#: lib/game_surfaces/taboo_surface.rb:16
msgid "Approve this turn"
msgstr "Aprobar este turno"

msgid "Apă-Canal"
msgstr "Apă-Canal"

#: games/axel_pong.rb:28 lib/axel_pong/client.rb:451
msgid "Arcade"
msgstr "Arcade"

msgid "Arcade: shields and invisible ball"
msgstr "Arcade: escudos y pelota invisible"

msgid "Arrow keys and Enter choose the current action, such as rolling, buying or answering an offer. I reads positions, T the phase and turn, C your cash, S finances, F the current deed, D unowned properties and Shift+D the whole board. V lists your holdings; Shift+V the others' holdings."
msgstr "Usa las flechas y Enter para elegir la acción actual, como lanzar los dados, comprar o responder a una oferta. I lee las posiciones; T, la fase y el turno; C, tu efectivo; S, las finanzas; F, el título de propiedad actual; D, las propiedades sin dueño, y Shift+D, todo el tablero. V enumera tus posesiones; Shift+V, las de los demás."

msgid "Arrow keys browse the board. Enter selects your piece, then Enter on the destination attempts the move. Promotion opens a choice list. V reads legal destinations for the inspected piece; E reads pieces attacking the inspected field, including an empty field; C identifies each player's colour."
msgstr "Usa las flechas para recorrer el tablero. Enter selecciona tu pieza; después, Enter sobre la casilla de destino intenta realizar el movimiento. La promoción abre una lista de opciones. V lee los destinos legales de la pieza examinada; E lee las piezas que atacan la casilla examinada, aunque esté vacía; C indica el color de cada jugador."

msgid "Arrow keys browse your hand. Enter plays the current card, or the prepared packet, opening any required declaration list. Shift+Enter adds or removes a card from the packet in selection order; Enter also includes the current card if it is not selected yet. P reads the prepared packet in selection order; Shift+P clears it. Space draws, or ends the turn after an ordinary draw. If you cannot defend against a draw or waiting penalty, the game accepts it automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "Arrow keys browse your hand. Enter plays the current card, or the prepared packet, opening any required declaration list. Shift+Enter adds or removes a card from the packet in selection order; Enter also includes the current card if it is not selected yet. P reads the prepared packet in selection order; Shift+P clears it. Space draws, or ends the turn after an ordinary draw. To accept a waiting penalty, use its separate action with Enter."
msgstr "Usa las flechas para recorrer tu mano. Enter juega la carta actual o el grupo de cartas preparado y abre la lista de declaraciones que sea necesaria. Shift+Enter añade o quita una carta del grupo siguiendo el orden de selección; Enter también incluye la carta actual si aún no está seleccionada. P lee el grupo de cartas preparado en el orden de selección; Shift+P lo vacía. Espacio roba una carta o termina el turno después de un robo normal. Para aceptar una penalización de espera, usa su acción independiente con Enter."

msgid "Arrow keys browse your hand. Enter plays the current card, or the prepared packet, opening any required declaration list. Shift+Enter adds or removes a card from the packet in selection order; Enter also includes the current card if it is not selected yet. Prepared cards are marked in the list, and P reminds you of that. Shift+P clears the packet. Space draws, or ends the turn after an ordinary draw. To accept a waiting penalty, use its separate action with Enter."
msgstr "Usa las flechas para recorrer tu mano. Enter juega la carta actual o el grupo de cartas preparado y abre la lista de declaraciones que sea necesaria. Shift+Enter añade o quita una carta del grupo siguiendo el orden de selección; Enter también incluye la carta actual si aún no está seleccionada. Las cartas preparadas aparecen marcadas en la lista, y P te lo recuerda. Shift+P vacía el grupo de cartas. Espacio roba una carta o termina el turno después de un robo normal. Para aceptar una penalización de espera, usa su acción independiente con Enter."

msgid "Arrow keys browse your hand; Enter plays a card and opens colour or opponent choices when needed. Space draws. C reads the top card and effective colour. S reads scores, T the turn, U declares or catches UNO, F challenges Wild Draw Four, B responds to a buzzer and G reads the pending penalty."
msgstr "Usa las flechas para recorrer tu mano; Enter juega una carta y abre las opciones de color u oponente cuando es necesario. Espacio roba una carta. C lee la carta superior y el color vigente. S lee las puntuaciones; T, el turno; U anuncia UNO o señala que alguien no lo ha anunciado; F desafía un comodín roba cuatro; B responde a un pulsador, y G lee la penalización pendiente."

msgid "Arrow keys browse your hand; Enter plays a card and opens colour or opponent choices when needed. Space draws. C reads the top card, V the current colour, E reads every player's card count, S the scores, T the turn, U declares or catches UNO, F challenges Wild Draw Four, B responds to a buzzer and G reads the pending penalty."
msgstr "Usa las flechas para recorrer tu mano; Enter juega una carta y abre las opciones de color u oponente cuando es necesario. Espacio roba una carta. C lee la carta superior; V, el color actual; E, el número de cartas de cada jugador; S, las puntuaciones; T, el turno; U anuncia UNO o señala que alguien no lo ha anunciado; F desafía un comodín roba cuatro; B responde a un pulsador, y G lee la penalización pendiente."

msgid "Arrow keys browse your hand; Enter plays a card and opens colour or opponent choices when needed. Space draws. C reads the top card, V the current colour, S the scores, T the turn, U declares or catches UNO, F challenges Wild Draw Four, B responds to a buzzer and G reads the pending penalty."
msgstr "Usa las flechas para recorrer tu mano; Enter juega una carta y abre las opciones de color u oponente cuando es necesario. Espacio roba una carta. C lee la carta superior; V, el color actual; S, las puntuaciones; T, el turno; U anuncia UNO o señala que alguien no lo ha anunciado; F desafía un comodín roba cuatro; B responde a un pulsador, y G lee la penalización pendiente."

msgid "Arrow keys inspect every field. In numbered notation the light, unplayable fields make a sound without a spoken name. Enter selects a piece; another Enter chooses its destination. V reads possible moves. K visits your kings and Shift+K the opponent's kings. C reads colours; T reads the turn."
msgstr "Usa las flechas para examinar todas las casillas. En la notación numérica, las casillas claras, que no se pueden jugar, emiten un sonido sin que se lea su nombre. Enter selecciona una pieza; otro Enter elige su destino. V lee los movimientos posibles. K recorre tus damas y Shift+K las del oponente. C lee los colores; T lee el turno."

msgid "Arrow keys inspect fields; Enter places your mark on the selected empty field during your turn. T announces the turn. You can also enter /a1 in chat to play on A1; this is a move command, not a chat message."
msgstr "Usa las flechas para examinar las casillas; Enter coloca tu marca en la casilla vacía seleccionada durante tu turno. T anuncia el turno. También puedes escribir /a1 en el chat para jugar en A1; es un comando de movimiento, no un mensaje de chat."

msgid "Arrow keys: browse squares. Enter on your piece selects it; Enter on its destination attempts the move. Promotion opens a choice list."
msgstr "Flechas: recorrer las casillas. Enter sobre tu pieza la selecciona; Enter sobre su destino intenta realizar el movimiento. La promoción abre una lista de opciones."

msgid "Arrow keys: inspect squares. Enter: place a disc on the selected square."
msgstr "Flechas: examinar las casillas. Enter: colocar una ficha en la casilla seleccionada."

msgid "Arrow keys: inspect squares. Enter: select a piece, then its destination. Choose each jump of a multiple capture separately."
msgstr "Flechas: examinar las casillas. Enter: seleccionar una pieza y después su destino. Elige por separado cada salto de una captura múltiple."

msgid "Arrow keys: inspect the board. Enter: drop a piece into the selected column, regardless of the row you are inspecting."
msgstr "Flechas: examinar el tablero. Enter: dejar caer una ficha en la columna seleccionada, independientemente de la fila que estés examinando."

msgid "Arrow keys: move around the board and read the selected square."
msgstr "Flechas: desplazarte por el tablero y leer la casilla seleccionada."

msgid "Arrows and Enter: choose a gift destination, public card, Church effect or auction action. R: enter another bid. To pay, Shift+Enter selects or removes cards from a packet and Enter submits it. Do not pay accepts the penalty instead. Escape clears the payment packet."
msgstr "Flechas y Enter: elegir el destino de una donación, una carta pública, un efecto de Iglesia o una acción de subasta. R: introducir otra puja. Para pagar, Shift+Enter selecciona o quita cartas de un grupo y Enter lo envía. No pagar acepta la penalización en su lugar. Escape vacía el grupo de cartas para el pago."

msgid "Arrows and Enter: choose and play a card, then a colour or player if required. Space: draw. U: announce or catch UNO. B: respond to a buzzer. F: challenge Wild Draw Four."
msgstr "Flechas y Enter: elegir y jugar una carta y, después, un color o un jugador si es necesario. Espacio: robar una carta. U: anunciar UNO o señalar que alguien no lo ha anunciado. B: responder a un pulsador. F: desafiar un comodín roba cuatro."

msgid "Arrows and Enter: choose the current action. I: player positions and field numbers. T: turn and phase. C: your cash. S: finances. F: current deed."
msgstr "Flechas y Enter: elegir la acción actual. I: posiciones de los jugadores y números de las casillas. T: turno y fase. C: tu efectivo. S: finanzas. F: título de propiedad actual."

msgid "Arrows browse A1–O15. Enter on an empty field opens your available tiles; choose one with arrows and press Enter to place it. A blank asks for its letter. Escape closes the choice without changing the draft. The cursor stays on the chosen field. Keys 1–7 only read individual rack positions; C reads the whole rack."
msgstr "Usa las flechas para recorrer A1–O15. Enter sobre una casilla vacía abre la lista de tus fichas disponibles; elige una con las flechas y pulsa Enter para colocarla. Si es un comodín, se te pedirá que elijas su letra. Escape cierra la selección sin cambiar el borrador. El cursor permanece en la casilla elegida. Las teclas 1–7 solo leen posiciones individuales del atril; C lee todo el atril."

msgid "Arrows browse A1–O15. H/V enter horizontal/vertical writing; N returns to navigation. Shift+letter places that letter while writing or finds it while navigating. Enter selects a rack tile for the current field. Keys 1–7 read rack positions; Shift+1–7 place them while writing or swap two chosen positions while navigating. Blank selection asks for its letter."
msgstr "Usa las flechas para recorrer A1–O15. H/V activan la escritura horizontal/vertical; N vuelve a la navegación. Shift+letra coloca esa letra al escribir o la busca al navegar. Enter selecciona una ficha del atril para la casilla actual. Las teclas 1–7 leen las posiciones del atril; Shift+1–7 las colocan al escribir o intercambian dos posiciones elegidas al navegar. Al seleccionar un comodín, se te pide que elijas su letra."

msgid "Arrows browse the hand. Enter offers matching melds, even when there is just one. If none matches it offers Discard and Cancel. Delete discards directly. N starts a meld; Enter selects or deselects cards in order; another N keeps that group and starts the next. F submits all prepared groups. P reads them and their value; Shift+P edits or removes a group. Escape cancels the current local choice or unsubmitted draft."
msgstr "Usa las flechas para recorrer la mano. Enter ofrece las combinaciones compatibles, aunque solo haya una. Si no hay ninguna, ofrece Descartar y Cancelar. Supr descarta directamente. N inicia una combinación; Enter selecciona o deselecciona cartas en orden; otro N conserva ese grupo e inicia el siguiente. F envía todos los grupos preparados. P los lee junto con su valor; Shift+P edita o elimina un grupo. Escape cancela la selección local actual o el borrador sin enviar."

msgid "Arrows browse the target and five forbidden words. Enter starts the turn or confirms a guess for the describing player; P skips, B buzzes for opponents. C reads the card; 1 reads the target and 2–6 the forbidden words. R reads remaining time, S team scores, T the describing player and team. Guessers and observers cannot use card-reading shortcuts. In review, Enter on a card lets the master correct its result; a separate button approves the turn. These keys do not act in chat."
msgstr "Usa las flechas para recorrer la palabra que hay que adivinar y las cinco palabras prohibidas. Enter inicia el turno o confirma un acierto para quien da las pistas; P pasa a la siguiente carta y B hace sonar el pulsador para los oponentes. C lee la carta; 1 lee la palabra que hay que adivinar, y 2–6, las palabras prohibidas. R lee el tiempo restante; S, las puntuaciones de los equipos; T, la persona que da las pistas y su equipo. Quienes adivinan y los espectadores no pueden usar los atajos de lectura de cartas. Durante la revisión, Enter sobre una carta permite al anfitrión de la mesa corregir su resultado; un botón aparte aprueba el turno. Estas teclas no actúan en el chat."

msgid "Arrows choose a tile; Enter opens the train list if that tile has any legal destination. The list includes every train, even closed ones, so you can make a conscious choice. Enter on an unavailable destination explains a closed train, a mismatch or the required double and its owner. If the tile cannot go anywhere, the game says so without opening the list. Escape returns to the same tile."
msgstr "Usa las flechas para elegir una ficha; Enter abre la lista de trenes si la ficha tiene algún destino legal. La lista incluye todos los trenes, incluso los cerrados, para que puedas elegir con conocimiento de causa. Enter sobre un destino no disponible explica si el tren está cerrado, si la ficha no encaja o cuál es el doble obligatorio y a quién pertenece. Si la ficha no se puede colocar en ningún sitio, el juego lo anuncia sin abrir la lista. Escape vuelve a la misma ficha."

#: games/three_five_eight.rb:95
msgid "Arrows: browse cards or available commands."
msgstr ""

