msgid "Arrows: browse cards or colour choices."
msgstr "Flechas: explora las cartas o los colores disponibles."

#: games/rummy_ui.rb:146
msgid "Arrows: browse cards or combinations."
msgstr "Flechas: explora las cartas o las combinaciones."

#: games/makao.rb:93 games/ninety_nine.rb:95 games/spades.rb:231
msgid "Arrows: browse cards."
msgstr "Flechas: recorre las cartas."

msgid "Arrows: browse cards. Enter: play the current card or prepared packet, choosing a declaration if needed."
msgstr "Flechas: recorrer las cartas. Enter: jugar la carta actual o el grupo de cartas preparado y elegir una declaración si es necesario."

#: games/farkle.rb:55
msgid "Arrows: browse scoring combinations, Roll and Bank."
msgstr "Flechas: recorre las combinaciones que puntúan, Lanzar y Guardar puntos."

#: games/battleship.rb:68 games/checkers.rb:123 games/chess.rb:65 games/reversi.rb:57 games/tic_tac_toe.rb:36
msgid "Arrows: browse squares."
msgstr "Flechas: explorar las casillas."

#: games/biblios.rb:74
msgid "Arrows: browse the available cards or actions."
msgstr "Flechas: recorrer las cartas o acciones disponibles."

#: games/four_in_a_row.rb:37
msgid "Arrows: browse the board."
msgstr "Flechas: recorre el tablero."

#: games/taboo_ui.rb:94
msgid "Arrows: browse the card or review list when visible to you."
msgstr "Flechas: recorrer la carta o la lista de revisión cuando puedas verlas."

msgid "Arrows: browse your hand. Enter: play the selected card, or choose the value of an ace or ten. Escape: leave that choice without playing."
msgstr "Flechas: recorrer tu mano. Enter: jugar la carta seleccionada o elegir el valor de un as o un diez. Escape: salir de esa selección sin jugar."

msgid "Arrows: choose Roll or Bank."
msgstr "Flechas: elegir Lanzar o Guardar puntos."

#: games/tysiac.rb:103
msgid "Arrows: choose a bid, talon card or trick card."
msgstr "Flechas: elegir una puja, una carta de la reserva o una carta para la baza."

#: games/quiz_party.rb:93
msgid "Arrows: choose a category or answer."
msgstr "Flechas: elige una categoría o una respuesta."

msgid "Arrows: choose a category or answer. Enter: submit the highlighted choice. T: read the question. Ctrl+T: remaining answer time. S: scores. V: round summary. Ctrl+F1: rules and shortcuts. Escape: return to the table."
msgstr "Flechas: elegir una categoría o respuesta. Enter: enviar la opción resaltada. T: leer la pregunta. Ctrl+T: tiempo restante para responder. S: puntuaciones. V: resumen de la ronda. Ctrl+F1: reglas y atajos. Escape: volver a la mesa."

#: games/yahtzee.rb:76
msgid "Arrows: choose a scoring category."
msgstr "Flechas: elige una categoría de puntuación."

#: games/mexican_train.rb:125
msgid "Arrows: choose a tile or train."
msgstr "Flechas: elegir una ficha o un tren."

#: games/domino.rb:162
msgid "Arrows: choose a tile."
msgstr "Flechas: elegir una ficha."

msgid "Arrows: choose a tile. Enter: play it. G selects the left end and D the right end for tiles that fit both. This is a remembered preference, initially right; the keys do not play a tile themselves. If only one end fits, Enter uses it regardless of the preference."
msgstr "Flechas: elegir una ficha. Enter: jugarla. G selecciona el extremo izquierdo y D el derecho para las fichas que encajan en ambos. Esta preferencia se recuerda y al principio es el derecho; las teclas no juegan una ficha por sí solas. Si solo encaja en un extremo, Enter lo utiliza independientemente de la preferencia."

#: games/ludo.rb:85
msgid "Arrows: choose an available pawn move."
msgstr "Flechas: elige un movimiento disponible para una ficha."

#: games/cat_head_tail.rb:39
msgid ""
"Arrows: choose an option.\n"
"Enter: confirm the selection.\n"
"S: read scores.\n"
"C: read the number of points in hand.\n"
"T: check whose turn it is."
msgstr ""
"Flechas: elegir una opción.\n"
"Enter: confirmar la selección.\n"
"S: leer las puntuaciones.\n"
"C: leer los puntos acumulados en el turno.\n"
"T: consultar de quién es el turno."

#: games/monopoly.rb:106
msgid "Arrows: choose the current action or property."
msgstr "Flechas: elige la acción o la propiedad actual."

#: games/poker.rb:120
msgid "Arrows: during exchange, choose a card."
msgstr "Flechas: durante el cambio, elegir una carta."

#: games/categories.rb:106
msgid "Arrows: during review, select a grade."
msgstr "Flechas: durante la evaluación, selecciona una valoración."

msgid "Arrows: move around A1–O15. Enter on an empty field: choose a rack tile, then Enter to place it. A blank also asks for a letter. Escape cancels the choice. Backspace removes your unsubmitted tile under the cursor; Z clears the whole draft. F submits it."
msgstr "Flechas: desplazarte por A1–O15. Enter sobre una casilla vacía: elegir una ficha del atril y después Enter para colocarla. Si es un comodín, también se te pide una letra. Escape cancela la selección. Retroceso quita la ficha tuya que esté bajo el cursor y aún no hayas enviado; Z borra todo el borrador. F lo envía."

#: games/scrabble_ui.rb:64
msgid "Arrows: move around the board."
msgstr "Flechas: muévete por el tablero."

msgid "As an observer, press 1 in the Pong playfield to listen from the first player's end, or 2 to listen from the second player's end. The game confirms the player's name. This changes only your listening perspective and score order; it does not let you move either paddle. The choice stays in place between points. The keys do not select a perspective while you are typing in chat or reading history."
msgstr "Como espectador, pulsa 1 en el área de juego de Pong para escuchar desde el lado del primer jugador, o 2 para hacerlo desde el lado del segundo. El juego confirma el nombre del jugador. Esto solo cambia tu perspectiva de escucha y el orden de la puntuación; no te permite mover ninguna de las palas. La elección se mantiene entre puntos. Las teclas no seleccionan una perspectiva mientras escribes en el chat o lees el historial."

#: games/axel_pong.rb:283
msgid "As an observer, use the number keys in the Pong playfield to choose a player's perspective: 1 selects the first player, 2 the second, and in Doubles 3 the third and 4 the fourth. The numbers follow the player order in the match, not the teams. The game confirms the player's name. This changes only your listening perspective and the order of the spoken score after a point; it does not let you move any paddle. The choice stays in place between points. The keys do not select a perspective while you are typing in chat or reading history."
msgstr ""

msgid "As soon as a player acquires a Church card, the game is put on hold while the card is played and then discarded. A Church card is acquired when the active player keeps it for himself, when another player takes it from the public space, or when it is won at auction. A Church card placed in the Auction pile is not played at that point."
msgstr ""

msgid "Assess every answer before finishing."
msgstr "Evalúa todas las respuestas antes de terminar."

#: __app.rb:2613
msgid "Assign automatically"
msgstr "Asignar automáticamente"

#: lib/game_room_screens.rb:374 lib/game_room_screens.rb:379
msgid "Assign or edit"
msgstr "Asignar o editar"

msgid "Assign ten table presets to Ctrl+1 through Ctrl+0 in Game Room > Settings > Widget > Quick table creation. Select a shortcut and choose Assign or edit, then select the game, its options and table privacy, and name the preset. Return to Settings and choose Save; Cancel discards the edits. Pressing the shortcut on the widget creates the table without starting the match. Presets are saved locally; the shortcuts work only on the widget."
msgstr "Asigna diez configuraciones de mesa a los atajos de Ctrl+1 a Ctrl+0 en Game Room > Ajustes > Widget > Creación rápida de mesas. Selecciona un atajo y elige Asignar o editar; después, selecciona el juego, sus opciones y la privacidad de la mesa, y da un nombre a la configuración. Vuelve a Ajustes y elige Guardar; Cancelar descarta los cambios. Al pulsar el atajo en el widget se crea la mesa sin iniciar la partida. Las configuraciones se guardan localmente; los atajos solo funcionan en el widget."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:172
msgid "Assign ten table presets to Ctrl+1 through Ctrl+0 in Game Room > Settings > Widget. Tab to the Table shortcuts list at the end of that section. Select a shortcut with the arrows, press Enter, choose a game and confirm its options and table privacy. The assignment is saved immediately; Cancel in Settings does not undo it. The shortcuts work only on the widget and create a table without starting the match. Assignments are saved locally."
msgstr "Asigna diez configuraciones de mesa a los atajos de Ctrl+1 a Ctrl+0 en Game Room > Ajustes > Widget. Usa Tab para llegar a la lista Atajos de mesas al final de esa sección. Selecciona un atajo con las flechas, pulsa Enter, elige un juego y confirma sus opciones y la privacidad de la mesa. La asignación se guarda inmediatamente; Cancelar en Ajustes no la deshace. Los atajos solo funcionan en el widget y crean una mesa sin iniciar la partida. Las asignaciones se guardan localmente."

#: games/poker.rb:84
msgid "At showdown, your hand is the best five-card combination you can make from your two cards and the five on the board. You may use both private cards, just one, or neither. For example, if the best five cards are all on the board, everyone still contesting that pot has access to the same combination."
msgstr ""

msgid "At the beginning of each two-point service block, the game announces who will serve against whom. After the spoken announcement, the pause is twice the normal Single serve delay: 5.4 seconds instead of 2.7. The second serve uses the normal Single delay without repeating the announcement. You can move your paddle during the break, but serving requires a fresh press when the break ends. S reads Team A and Team B, both partners' names and the scores, separated by punctuation. T reads the server, receiver and connection status; C still reads your own paddle position."
msgstr ""

#: games/axel_pong.rb:264
msgid "At the beginning of each two-point service block, the game announces who will serve against whom. After the spoken announcement, there is the same 2.7-second serve delay as in Single. The second serve uses the normal Single delay without repeating the announcement. You can move your paddle during the break, but serving requires a fresh press when the break ends. S reads Team A and Team B, both partners' names and the scores, separated by punctuation. T reads the server, receiver and connection status; C still reads your own paddle position."
msgstr ""

msgid "At the end, subtract each player's unused tile values. If someone emptied their rack with an empty bag, add the others' unused values to that player's score. With a blocked board there is no such bonus. Blanks cost zero. The highest adjusted score wins; equal highest scores share the result. Save only after submitting or cancelling the local draft."
msgstr ""

#: games/ludo.rb:347
msgid "At the finish: %{count} of %{total} pawns"
msgstr "En la meta: %{count} de %{total} fichas"

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:143
msgid "At the start of Battleship, each player can choose random or manual fleet placement. Random placement follows the selected fleet and ship-spacing rules."
msgstr "Al comenzar Hundir la flota, cada jugador puede elegir entre colocar su flota al azar o manualmente. La colocación aleatoria respeta la flota elegida y las reglas de separación entre barcos."

#: games/rummy_ui.rb:120
msgid "At the start of each round, everyone must make their own first meld. Its minimum value defaults to 30 points and can be set from 15 to 90. You may prepare several new combinations from your own hand and submit them together to reach that value. A single combination below the threshold is not enough just because you hope to add another later."
msgstr ""

msgid "Ataturk Hava alani"
msgstr "Ataturk Hava alani"

#: games/makao.rb:133
msgid "Attacking kings"
msgstr "Reyes de ataque"

#: games/makao.rb:80
msgid "Attacking kings introduces a separate five-card attack. The king of spades starts it; the king of hearts can answer it and add five more. Thus spades followed by hearts makes the next player draw ten, unless they defend again. It does not reverse play. The other kings are ordinary cards, and a king attack is not combined with a two-or-three attack."
msgstr ""

#: games/krowa_support/leaderboards.rb:189 games/krowa_support/leaderboards.rb:71 games/krowa_support/presentation.rb:71
