msgstr "Intentos"

#: games/krowa_support/presentation.rb:201
msgid "Attempts: %{count}. %{status}"
msgstr "Intentos: %{count}. %{status}"

#: games/monopoly.rb:683
msgid "Auction begins: %{property}."
msgstr "Comienza la subasta: %{property}."

#: games/monopoly.rb:145
msgid "Auction decision time"
msgstr "Tiempo para decidir en la subasta"

#: games/monopoly.rb:152
msgid "Auction decision time cannot be negative."
msgstr "El tiempo para decidir en la subasta no puede ser negativo."

#: games/monopoly.rb:144
msgid "Auction decision time in seconds; 0 means no limit"
msgstr "Tiempo para decidir en la subasta, en segundos; 0 significa sin límite"

msgid "Auction decision time is entered in seconds. The default 0 means no time limit. A positive value gives each bidder that much time for one decision; running out of time means passing. Each accepted bid or pass starts a fresh limit for the next bidder. B lets you enter your own total purchase offer, higher than the current bid and no higher than your cash. Enter or G still places the suggested next bid."
msgstr ""

#: games/monopoly.rb:67
msgid "Auction decision time is the number of seconds for one bid or pass. Zero, the default, gives unlimited time. A positive limit starts afresh for the next bidder after every accepted decision; exceeding it means an automatic pass. B lets you enter a total purchase bid, above the current bid and within your cash. Enter or G accepts the suggested next bid. You cannot save the game during an auction."
msgstr ""

#: games/monopoly.rb:963
msgid "Auction ended without a sale: %{property}."
msgstr "La subasta ha terminado sin venta: %{property}."

msgid "Auction, transfer and play keys"
msgstr "Teclas de subasta, transferencia y juego"

#: games/tysiac.rb:1568
msgid "Auction: %{bids}."
msgstr "Subasta: %{bids}."

#: games/biblios.rb:1299
msgid "Auctioned: %{card}. %{bid}"
msgstr "En subasta: %{card}. %{bid}"

#: games/audio_ball.rb:17
msgid "Audio Ball"
msgstr "Audio Ball"

msgid "Audio Ball is an audio game for exactly two players, one against one. Play another person or a bot. Classic is currently the only mode. You score a point when the opponent fails to defend your shot. Headphones help you follow the ball and distinguish the three shot sounds."
msgstr ""

#: games/audio_ball.rb:188
msgid "Audio Ball is an audio game played one against one, with another person or a bot. In Classic mode, you catch the opponent's shots and send the ball back. You score a point when the opponent misses. There are three types of shot, each with a distinct sound. Listen to the sound to choose the matching defence."
msgstr ""

msgid "Audio Ball keyboard shortcuts"
msgstr "Atajos de teclado de Audio Ball"

#: games/audio_ball.rb:168
msgid "Audio Ball playfield"
msgstr "Área de juego de Audio Ball"

#: games/audio_ball.rb:159
msgid "Audio Ball requires exactly two players."
msgstr "Audio Ball requiere exactamente dos jugadores."

#: games/audio_ball.rb:22
msgid "Audio Ball settings"
msgstr "Ajustes de Audio Ball"

#: lib/audio_tutorial.rb:53 lib/game_room_screens.rb:492
msgid "Audio tutorial"
msgstr "Tutorial de audio"

#: lib/axel_pong/settings.rb:15
msgid "Automatic return (only for you)"
msgstr "Devolución automática (solo para ti)"

msgid "Automatic return for both players"
msgstr "Devolución automática para ambos jugadores"

msgid "Automatic return for both players is off by default. When enabled, the paddle hits a reachable ball automatically near its own end. You still position the paddle and serve yourself. The setting applies equally to both human players."
msgstr ""

#: games/axel_pong.rb:258
msgid "Automatic return is a personal setting, off by default. When enabled, your paddle returns a reachable ball automatically near your end. You still position the paddle and serve yourself. Open Pong settings with Ctrl+P to change it; your opponent chooses independently."
msgstr ""

#: lib/game_surfaces/piece_board.rb:599
msgid "Available moves from %{field}: %{moves}."
msgstr "Movimientos disponibles desde %{field}: %{moves}."

#: games/axel_pong.rb:15 lib/game_room_screens.rb:175
msgid "Axel Pong"
msgstr "Axel Pong"

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:240
msgid "Axel Pong adds Custom score, with a field for 2 to 999 points, and Unlimited, which keeps the match going without a score limit. Both options work in Singles and Doubles, including matches with bots. Finite matches still require a two-point lead."
msgstr "Axel Pong añade Número personalizado, con un campo para introducir entre 2 y 999 puntos, y Sin límite, que permite seguir jugando sin límite de puntos. Ambas opciones funcionan en partidas individuales y de dobles, también con bots. Las partidas con límite siguen requiriendo dos puntos de ventaja."

#: lib/game_room_changelog.rb:266
msgid "Axel Pong and Audio Ball still pause when you switch to another ELTEN window: their controls require the game field to be active. The background-play changes apply to the other games."
msgstr "Axel Pong y Audio Ball se siguen pausando al cambiar a otra ventana de ELTEN: sus controles requieren que el campo de juego esté activo. Los cambios para jugar en segundo plano se aplican a los demás juegos."

#: games/axel_pong.rb:252
msgid "Axel Pong is an audio paddle game for two players, or four players in doubles. Move your paddle along your end of the court and return the ball before it passes you. You score one point when your opponent misses. You can play with other people or add bots to the table. Headphones make it much easier to hear where the ball is."
msgstr ""

msgid "Axel Pong is an audio paddle game for two players. Move your paddle along your end of the court and return the ball before it passes you. You score one point when your opponent misses. You can play with another person or add a bot to the table. Headphones make it much easier to hear where the ball is."
msgstr ""

#: games/axel_pong.rb:250 lib/game_room_changelog.rb:169
msgid "Axel Pong is not an original project by papierek. The game was originally called Dragon-Pong, was later improved by Axel and balteam, and has now been ported to ELTEN with their permission."
msgstr "Axel Pong no es un proyecto original de papierek. El juego se llamaba Dragon-Pong originalmente, después Axel y balteam lo mejoraron y ahora se ha adaptado a ELTEN con su permiso."

#: games/mancala.rb:31
msgid "Ayoayo (keep sowing on from every pit that was not empty)"
msgstr "Ayoayo (continúa sembrando desde cada hoyo que no estuviera vacío)"

#: games/mancala.rb:65
msgid "Ayoayo skips the stores and the pit emptied for each sowing. If the last seed lands in a pit that already held seeds, take everything from that pit and continue sowing from there. This continuation is still part of your original move, even on the opposing side. It stops when your last seed lands in an empty pit."
msgstr ""

#: games/mancala.rb:64
msgid "Ayoayo: one move can continue through several pits"
msgstr ""

msgid "B during bidding: enter your declaration. Outside bidding: read the declarations. Arrows and Enter: choose and play a card."
msgstr "B durante la declaración de bazas: introducir tu declaración. Fuera de esa fase: leer las declaraciones. Flechas y Enter: elegir y jugar una carta."

msgid "B&O railroad"
msgstr "Ferrocarril B&O"

#: games/taboo_ui.rb:97
msgid "B: as an opponent, report a violation."
msgstr "B: como rival, notificar una infracción."

#: games/chess.rb:79
msgid "B: browse your bishops."
msgstr "B: recorre tus alfiles."

#: games/tysiac.rb:106
msgid "B: change the final contract before playing the first card."
msgstr "B: cambiar el contrato definitivo antes de jugar la primera carta."

#: games/monopoly.rb:125
msgid "B: during an auction, enter your own total bid."
msgstr "B: durante una subasta, introduce el importe total de tu puja."

#: games/spades.rb:233
msgid "B: during bidding, enter your bid; otherwise read the bids."
msgstr "B: durante las declaraciones, introducir tu declaración; en los demás casos, leer las declaraciones."

#: games/biblios.rb:85
msgid "B: read the current auction."
msgstr "B: leer la subasta actual."

#: games/uno.rb:125
msgid "B: respond to the buzzer."
msgstr "B: responde al pulsador."

#: __app.rb:1004 __app.rb:1048 __app.rb:1161 __app.rb:1673 __app.rb:1789 __app.rb:1974 __app.rb:907 games/krowa_support/leaderboards.rb:37 lib/game_room_screens.rb:497 lib/game_room_screens.rb:518 lib/game_screen.rb:1298 lib/game_screen.rb:378
msgid "Back"
msgstr "Volver"

msgid "Back to rule sections"
msgstr "Volver a las secciones de las reglas"

msgid "Back to the table"
msgstr "Volver a la mesa"

#: games/battleship.rb:57
msgid "Backspace cancels a marked first end. If no end is marked, it removes the last ship you placed. An invalid placement leaves the first end selected, so you can choose a different second end or cancel it. After the last ship, confirm that the fleet is ready. Declining takes back that last ship. Once confirmed, the fleet cannot be rearranged."
msgstr ""

msgid "Backspace removes your unsubmitted tile under the cursor; Z clears the whole draft; F submits it. Y previews words and points without checking the dictionary. I cycles free, alphabetic and vowel-first rack order, after clearing the draft. G opens tile exchange: arrows browse, Space selects, Enter confirms and Escape cancels. P passes. Exchange and pass ask before discarding a draft. L lists played words; E reads tile counts; S reads scores; T reads whose turn it is. These shortcuts do not act in chat."
msgstr "Retroceso quita la ficha tuya que esté bajo el cursor y aún no hayas enviado; Z borra todo el borrador; F lo envía. Y muestra una vista previa de las palabras y los puntos sin consultar el diccionario. I alterna entre el orden libre del atril, el alfabético y el de vocales primero, tras borrar el borrador. G abre el cambio de fichas: las flechas recorren la lista, Espacio selecciona, Enter confirma y Escape cancela. P pasa el turno. El cambio de fichas y pasar el turno piden confirmación antes de descartar un borrador. L enumera las palabras jugadas; E lee el número de fichas; S lee las puntuaciones; T lee de quién es el turno. Estos atajos no actúan en el chat."

