msgid "Food"
msgstr "Comida"

msgid "For a card that is not a Gold card, players bid by announcing how much Gold they are willing to pay, and the winner pays with any combination of Gold cards from her hand. A player may be forced to pay more than the bid, as there is no change. When a Gold card is auctioned, players bid the number of cards they wish to pay instead, and pay with any cards they wish."
msgstr ""

#: games/biblios.rb:66
msgid "For a category or Church card, bid an amount of Gold and pay with Gold cards. There is no change. If you bid 4 but pay with two Gold cards worth 3 each, you spend 6. For a Gold card, bid a number of cards instead: a bid of 2 means giving up two hand cards, which may be of any type. Choose the payment carefully, because useful library cards can also be spent this way."
msgstr ""

#: games/three_five_eight.rb:89
msgid "For a non-trump card, the recipient automatically returns their highest card of the same suit; if the received card is their only card of that suit, it simply returns. For a trump card, the recipient may instead return any non-trump card, or their highest trump. Exchanges are completed before the chooser takes the kitty."
msgstr ""

#: games/scrabble_ui.rb:53
msgid "For each new word, add the values of all its letters, including letters already on the board. A newly covered letter bonus doubles or triples that tile's value. After letter bonuses, apply the word bonuses to the whole word. Several word multipliers multiply together. For example, two double-word fields make the word worth four times its letter total."
msgstr ""

msgid "For example, rolling 4 and then 6 gives you ten turn points. Banking saves those ten and ends your turn. Rolling 1 instead loses the ten. If you roll 2 before that 1, you still lose the ten turn points, but keep the two points that went straight into your bank."
msgstr ""

#: games/mancala.rb:58
msgid "For example, sowing four seeds from A1 adds one each to B1, C1, D1 and E1. You do not choose their destinations separately. What happens when the last seed lands depends on the variant, so read the section for the game selected at your table."
msgstr ""

#: games/tysiac.rb:86
msgid "For example, suppose the unchosen talon contains an ace and a nine, and the bidder sets aside a king and a jack. Those four cards are worth 17 points. With the checkbox enabled, winning the last trick gives its winner these 17 points in addition to the points in the trick itself. With it disabled, those 17 points are not awarded."
msgstr ""

#: games/yahtzee.rb:71
msgid "For example, with 50 in Yahtzee you roll five threes. An unused Threes row takes 15. If Threes is already filled, the Joker may let you put 40 in Large straight instead. The additional 100 is awarded only if its separate bonus setting is on. There is no joker button or physical joker die to use."
msgstr ""

#: games/biblios.rb:55
msgid "For example, you might collect 12 points of Monks and beat an opponent's 10. If the Monk die shows 4 at the end, you receive 4 victory points, not 12. Gold cards pay for purchases, while Church cards change the dice. The game has two distinct halves: first the free distribution of gifts, then auctions."
msgstr ""

msgid "For the describer, Enter starts the turn or marks a correct guess, and P skips. For opponents, B reports a violation. Guessing teammates answer aloud without using these keys."
msgstr "Para quien describe, Enter inicia el turno o marca un acierto, y P salta la carta. Para los rivales, B notifica una infracción. Los compañeros que adivinan responden en voz alta sin usar estas teclas."

#: games/monopoly.rb:138
msgid "Forbid buying properties on the first board round"
msgstr "Prohibir la compra de propiedades durante la primera vuelta al tablero"

#: games/monopoly.rb:64
msgid "Forbid buying properties on the first board round is off by default. If enabled, each player must first pass Start once before an unowned field offers them a purchase. This is your own first trip around the board, not the first circuit of turns taken by the table."
msgstr ""

msgid "Forbid buying properties on the first board round is off by default. When enabled, each player must pass Start once before landing on an unowned property can offer a purchase. The restriction concerns that player's first lap, not one shared round of turns."
msgstr ""

#: games/domino.rb:31
msgid "Forbid drawing from the boneyard"
msgstr "Prohibir robar del pozo"

#: games/domino.rb:151
msgid "Forbid drawing in the boneyard turns this into a no-draw game. It disables the other drawing options: you must play a legal tile, or pass automatically if you have none. Undealt tiles remain unavailable. This setting is off by default."
msgstr ""

#: games/biblios.rb:1209
