#: games/cat_head_tail.rb:37
msgid ""
"It is a simple game based on PIG from RS Games containing several differences, which are described below:\n"
"First of all, instead of six, the die has eight sides.\n"
"1 loses all points collected so far and ends the turn;\n"
"2 is automatically added to the bank, but the same player may continue playing;\n"
"7 is Head (the cat's head), which does absolutely nothing;\n"
"8 is tail (the cat's tail), which randomly adds or subtracts 8 points.\n"
"The target score is selected when creating the table; the default is 100.\n"
"After the last player's turn in the round ends, the highest score wins. If several players have the same highest score, the game ends in a draw."
msgstr ""

#: games/scientific_war.rb:43
msgid "It is based on War, but you choose which card to play, so bluff and strategy matter. There is no random deal. Every player gets all thirteen cards of one suit, from two to ace, plus one joker, so everyone starts with the same cards. Two players play with hearts and spades. With more than four players a second deck is added, so some suits appear twice."
msgstr ""

#: games/poker.rb:459
msgid "It is not the card-exchange stage."
msgstr "No es la fase de cambio de cartas."

