msgid "You must cover double %{number} on %{player}'s train."
msgstr "Debes cubrir el doble %{number} en el tren de %{player}."

#: games/mexican_train.rb:164
msgid "You must cover double %{number} on the Mexican train."
msgstr "Debes cubrir el doble %{number} en el tren mexicano."

#: games/tysiac.rb:516
msgid "You must follow suit or play a trump when required."
msgstr "Debes seguir el palo o jugar un triunfo cuando sea obligatorio."

#: games/three_five_eight.rb:413
msgid "You must follow suit when you have a card of the led suit."
msgstr ""

msgid "You must follow the led suit whenever possible. If you cannot follow and a trump suit has been established, you must play a trump if you have one. Otherwise you may discard any card. Cards rank from strongest to weakest: ace, 10, king, queen, jack and 9."
msgstr ""

#: games/spades.rb:693
msgid "You must follow the suit that was led."
msgstr "Debes jugar una carta del palo de salida."

#: games/mancala.rb:62
msgid "You must not capture every seed left on the opposing side at once. Such a move may be played, but no capture occurs. If the opponent's row is empty before your turn, you must choose a sowing that feeds it when one exists. Otherwise the game ends, and each player keeps the seeds remaining on their own side."
msgstr ""

#: games/mancala.rb:255
msgid "You must put seeds into the other row."
msgstr "Debes poner semillas en la otra fila."

#: games/rummy_ui.rb:131
msgid "You need not return every borrowed card, but each one left unplayed at the end of the turn costs 300 points. Two retained cards therefore cost 600. This is charged once; on later turns those cards are ordinary hand cards. An equivalent copy can repay one borrowed card, not several. In normal scoring, taking a card also removes its previous meld value; putting it back awards its new meld value. Moving cards around is not a source of free repeated points."
msgstr ""

#: games/biblios.rb:368
msgid "You pick up %{card}."
msgstr "Recoges %{card}."

msgid "You place %{mark} on %{field}."
msgstr "Colocas %{mark} en %{field}."

msgid "You play the part of an abbot at the head of a monastery, seeking to amass the most illustrious library. The goal is to earn the most Victory Points by having a higher score in a category than anyone else."
